    // Code to handle successful download
}
```
Reason:
The absence of a `break;` statement after the successful download of cover art allows the loop to continue executing, which can lead to multiple downloads being attempted even after a successful one, potentially causing unintended behavior or errors.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if (coverBytes != null) {
    // Code to handle successful download
    break;
}
```
Reason:
Adding the `break;` statement ensures that once cover art is successfully downloaded, the loop terminates, preventing any further attempts to download additional covers, thus maintaining the intended logic of the method.

